# Internal dofollow, external nofollow

All site links must follow this policy:

- **Internal** (paths starting with `/`, `#`, or `https://www.thereputation360.com`): **dofollow** — no `rel` attribute, same tab (no `target="_blank"`).
- **External** (other `http(s)` URLs): **nofollow** — `target="_blank"` and `rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow"`.
- **mailto / tel / sms**: no `target` or `rel`.

## Always use `src/lib/internalLinkProps.js`

| Situation | Use |
|-----------|-----|
| Href may be internal or external | `anchorTabProps(href)` |
| Guaranteed internal only | `internalAnchorProps(href)` |
| Guaranteed external only | `externalAnchorProps(href)` |
| Calendly consultation CTA | `calendlyNewTabProps` from `scheduling.js` |
| Constant for share / static HTML | `EXTERNAL_LINK_REL` |

```jsx
// ✅ GOOD — mixed or unknown href
<a href={href} {...anchorTabProps(href)}>{label}</a>

// ✅ GOOD — known external URL
<a href={url} {...externalAnchorProps(url)}>{label}</a>

// ✅ GOOD — known internal path
<a href="/about" {...internalAnchorProps("/about")}>About</a>

// ❌ BAD — hardcoded rel without nofollow on external links
<a href="https://example.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">...</a>

// ❌ BAD — nofollow on internal navigation
<a href="/blog/foo" rel="nofollow">...</a>
```

## Blogs and rich text links

- **React rich text / in-article links**: `DiyInternalLink`, `Pack20RichText`, or spread `anchorTabProps(href)` — never hardcode `rel`.
- **Pack20 / rich text data**: mark outbound URLs with `external: true`.
- **index.html / boot snippets**: external anchors use `rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow"`.

`App.jsx` runs `applyNewTabToAnchors()` on the live DOM, but still use helpers in source so SSR and client code stay correct.

## CI

`npm run verify:links` fails if source files hardcode `rel="noopener noreferrer"` without `nofollow`.
